Z||000000||Stoic||02-09-2001||03:17 PM||||My car has been driving very "loose" the past while.  It pretty much goes where it wants to, and is often quite the handful.  I have the problem narrowed to the driver side rear.  When I hit pot holes it makes a horrible knock in that area.  I have put in new ball joints, and bearings thinking that was the problem but no dice. Any ideas would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||5
Z||000001||lou_dias||02-09-2001||03:19 PM||||worn out bushings is what did it for me, also check your tire pressures.<p>[This message has been edited by lou_dias (edited 02-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||151 in. of love||02-09-2001||05:24 PM||||It may be a strike-out bumber that sits around your shock and softens the force when fully compressed. It may also just be time for some new shocks/struts. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||02-09-2001||10:24 PM||||Are the rod ends at each end of the toe link in good shape?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Stoic||02-10-2001||02:01 PM||||I was actually thinking it might be the rod ends.  The mufflerman told me they need to be done soon, but they're o.k. now.  If it is that then I have to figure out where to get them.  The GM dealership here and the suspension places all tell me that they can't get them.  Any ideas on where I could get them?  I want new ones, not used.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||6
